ons/runs/33867172807/rerun","previous_attempt_url":null,"workflow_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Hem60/PatelHem/actions/workflows/350053545","head_commit":{"id":"8350559894f1f41748e03d6cb4e643ad818f53cc","tree_id":"edf537080fc2f47c9abdfade6a16e1975ace4aef","message":"Freeze the regression fixture so a survey can publish\n\nThe first survey run collected cleanly, scored six repositories and composed\nthe catalogue — then failed the test gate and refused to commit. The gate was\nright to stop; the test was wrong.\n\nregression.test.ts read phase00/out/raw.json, which is exactly the file the\nsurvey overwrites with a fresh collection. So it compared today's account\nagainst expectations pinned to 2026-08-26 and broke on changes that were all\ncorrect: vakil gained a commit (27 -> 28) and PatelHem appeared as a sixth\nentry. Six assertions failed without a line of engine code moving, and a valid\nreading could not reach the site.\n\nA regression test pins CODE against KNOWN INPUT. If the input moves with the\naccount it is not a regression test, it is a diff against yesterday. The\nfixture is now a committed copy the survey never touches.\n\nRe-pinning is deliberate: overwrite the fixture and update the numbers in the\nsame commit.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","timestamp":"2026-09-04T11:15:20Z","author":{"name":"Hem Patel","email":"patelhem60@gmail.com"},"committer":{"name":"Hem Patel","email":"patelhem60@gmail.com"}},"repository":{"id":1356848983,"node_id":"R_kgDOUN_fVw","name":"PatelHem","full_name":"Hem60/PatelHem","private":false,"owner":{"login":"Hem60","id":227198061,"node_id":"U_kgDODYrEbQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/227198061?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hem60","html_url":"https://github.com/Hem60","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hem60/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hem60/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/user